invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the parser no longer bounds the extension count, so a ClientHello of
  16,383 empty extensions costs the duplicate check and the frozen digest's
  walk seconds of processor time before any key exists (docs/decisions.md
  59). test/srv_quic_retry_count_tests.h fills ngtcp2's two recorded hellos
  out with the same unknown extensions, so the frozen digest matches, and
  requires the second hello, one past SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX, to be
  refused with illegal_parameter. Only the count can refuse it.

--- old
    if (srv_ext_over_max(exts, exts_len)) {
--- new
    if (0 && srv_ext_over_max(exts, exts_len)) {
